    "campus": "Moulsham Street campus",
    "campusIllustrative": true,
    "startDate": "September 2026",
    "overview": "The course requires students to set up and run their own business. Assessment will be through both practical and written tasks. An office area will be provided for students and business dress is to be worn.\n\nMandatory units:\n\nThere are eight mandatory units, eight internally assessed and four externally assessed. Learn...",
    "studyOverviewHtml": "<p>The course requires students to set up and run their own business. Assessment will be through both practical and written tasks. An office area will be provided for students and business dress is to be worn.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Mandatory units</strong>:<br />\nThere are eight mandatory units, eight internally assessed and four externally assessed. Learners must complete and achieve at Pass grade or above for all units.</p>\n\n<p><br />\n<strong>Year 1 </strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Unit 1 Enterprise and Entrepreneurs</li>\n\t<li>Unit 2 Developing a Marketing Campaign</li>\n\t<li>Unit 3 Business and Personal Finance</li>\n\t<li>Unit 4 Launch and Run an Enterprise</li>\n\t<li>Unit 8 Entrepreneurship and Intrapreneurship in Practice</li>\n\t<li>Unit 9 Innovation and Enterprises</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Units 2 and 3 are externally assessed in Year 1</strong></p>\n\n<p><br />\n<strong>Year 2</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Unit 5 Survival and Growth</li>\n\t<li>Unit 6 Business Decision Making</li>\n\t<li>Unit 10 Recruitment and Selection Processes</li>\n\t<li>Unit 11 Marketing Communications (units are subject to change)</li>\n\t<li>Unit 12 Principles of Management</li>\n\t<li>Unit 13 Developing an Enterprise Strategy</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Units 6 and 12 are externally assessed in Year 2</strong></p>\n\n<p>We also collaborate with stakeholders, including Chelmsford City Council, to increase opportunities for learners to develop their entrepreneurial skills, such as through a Youth Innovation Event.\u00a0</p>",
    "courseForMeHtml": "<p>The National Extended Diploma is a 2-year, full-time course ideal for anyone who wants to progress to higher education courses in business areas before entering employment. It can also support learners who want to progress directly to employment. The BTEC Level 3 National Extended Diploma in Enterprise and Entrepreneurship is equivalent to 3 A Levels.</p>\n\n<p>The aims of the course are to learn how to:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Set up a supply chain.</li>\n\t<li>Learn how to communicate with customers.</li>\n\t<li>Opportunity to work closely with a business.</li>\n\t<li>Gain experience dealing with real business issues.</li>\n\t<li>Give learners the opportunity to plan, set up and run their own business through a structured programme of learning.</li>\n</ul>",
    "eligibilityHtml": "<ul>\n\t<li>4 GCSEs grades 9-4 including\u00a0English and Maths or successful achievement at a relevant level 2 vocational course.</li>\n\t<li>GCSE Business Studies or equivalent is desirable.</li>\n</ul>",
    "eligibilitySpecificHtml": "",
    "entryRequirements": [
      "4 GCSEs grades 9-4 including\u00a0English and Maths or successful achievement at a relevant level 2 vocational course.",
      "GCSE Business Studies or equivalent is desirable."
    ],
    "assessment": "There are a range of assessment methods across the course - internal and external.\n\nInternal assessments are assessed using a variety of styles including writing up findings of research, using case studies to explore different situations, carrying out projects and demonstrating practical skills.\n\nExternal assessments are either examinations \u2013 all learners take the same assessment at the same time, normally with a written outcome.\n\nSet tasks \u2013 learners take the assessment during a defined window and demonstrate understanding through completion of a vocational task.\n\nThe external units must be achieved at a Pass or above and learners are only permitted to re-sit the assessment once during their study programme.",
    "assessmentHtml": "<p>There are a range of assessment methods across the course - internal and external.</p>\n\n<p>Internal assessments are assessed using a variety of styles including writing up findings of research, using case studies to explore different situations, carrying out projects and demonstrating practical skills.</p>\n\n<p>External assessments are either examinations \u2013 all learners take the same assessment at the same time, normally with a written outcome.</p>\n\n<p>Set tasks \u2013 learners take the assessment during a defined window and demonstrate understanding through completion of a vocational task.</p>\n\n<p>The external units must be achieved at a Pass or above and learners are only permitted to re-sit the assessment once during their study programme.</p>",
