    "startDate": "September 2026",
    "overview": "Learners will develop an understanding of a broad range of issues relevant to the sector, including:\n\nPeople:\u00a0the importance and impact of people\n\nFinance:\u00a0how revenue and expenditure is tracked and controlled\n\nBusiness Context:\u00a0an overview of organisational cultures and values, different types of internal and external...",
    "studyOverviewHtml": "<p>Learners will develop an understanding of a broad range of issues relevant to the sector, including:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>People:\u00a0the importance and impact of people</li>\n\t<li>Finance:\u00a0how revenue and expenditure is tracked and controlled</li>\n\t<li>Business Context:\u00a0an overview of organisational cultures and values, different types of internal and external stakeholders, different forms of governance and the impact of organisations on society and the environment</li>\n\t<li>Project and Change Management:\u00a0an understanding of the common change management theories and models and how to support and improve projects</li>\n\t<li>Business Behaviours:\u00a0the importance of good communication and adapting social communication styles to professional standards\u00a0according to purpose, medium and audience</li>\n\t<li>Quality and Compliance: the importance of maintaining and improving quality in all aspects of public and private sector organisations</li>\n\t<li>Policies:\u00a0how organisations develop policies and why</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>In addition to the core content, each learner will also specialise in team leadership and management in the second year of the programme.</p>\n\n<p>We also collaborate with stakeholders, including Chelmsford City Council, to increase opportunities for learners to develop their entrepreneurial skills, such as through a Youth Innovation Event.\u00a0</p>",
    "courseForMeHtml": "<p>T Levels are a 2-year qualification that you can do after GCSEs as an alternative to A Levels, other post-16 courses or an apprenticeship.</p>\n\n<p>The curriculum has been designed with leading businesses and employers to ensure you're equipped with the necessary skills and knowledge the industry is looking for.</p>\n\n<p>You\u2019ll spend 80% of your time in the classroom and 20% on a 45-day placement with an employer to give you the skills and knowledge companies look for.</p>\n\n<p>Your industry placement also gives you the chance to learn what a real career is like while you continue your studies.\u00a0Like A Levels and BTECs, there are no tuition fees to study a T Level if you start before you are 19.</p>",
    "eligibilityHtml": "<p>4 GCSEs grades 9-4 including<strong>\u00a0</strong>English and Maths. GCSE Business Studies or equivalent is desirable.</p>",
