    "overview": "This 2-year full-time course is equivalent to 3 A levels. If you are interested in forensic studies, criminology, and psychology, then this course will give you an insight into those areas. The course includes studying core biology, chemistry, physics and science investigation skills to underpin scientific knowledge be...",
    "studyOverviewHtml": "<p>This 2-year full-time course is equivalent to 3 A levels. If you are interested in forensic studies, criminology, and psychology, then this course will give you an insight into those areas. The course includes studying core biology, chemistry, physics and science investigation skills to underpin scientific knowledge before specialising in forensic analysis and investigation.</p>\n\n<p>Units may include forensic archaeology, anthropology, forensic genetics, forensic fire investigation, and traffic accident investigation. You will also study criminal psychology and criminology as core elements of the course.\u00a0</p>",
    "courseForMeHtml": "<p>This course is designed for individuals who are fascinated by the intricacies of forensic evidence. If you have a passion for understanding the scientific and psychological aspects of crime, such as how\u00a0forensic evidence is gathered, processed, and analysed, as well as into the psychology of those who commit crimes, then this course could be for you. You will learn through activities based in our crime scene rooms, the laboratory, and the classroom, where a number of our activities are scenario-based. Overall, this Diploma in\u00a0Forensic and Criminal Investigation will provide you with a good understanding of the industry from various angles.</p>",
    "eligibilityHtml": "<p>4 GCSEs at\u00a0grades 9-4 including Maths and Science and English Language at grade 9-3.</p>\n\n<p>\u00a0</p>",
    "eligibilitySpecificHtml": "<p>Internal candidates should also have successful completion of current course to meet course entry requirements and meet College expectations regarding attendance and attitude</p>",
