    "studyOverviewHtml": "<p>This course is comprised of practical and theoretical elements to ensure upon completion, you have the necessary skills, understanding, and knowledge to progress to where you wish.</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><strong>30%</strong> of the course involves <strong>practical</strong> tasks in the workshop, building hand skills, basic requirements, and good practices for electrical installations.</li>\n\t<li><strong>70%</strong> of the course is <strong>theory </strong>on the safe working and health and safety, electrical installation practices, and knowledge of tools and equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>If you additionally have a passion for football, the course also offers the opportunity to take part in our Football Academy in conjunction with Billericay Town FC.</p>",
    "courseForMeHtml": "<p>This qualification allows you to acquire the knowledge and craft skills of electrical installation. It does not require occupational evidence from the workplace, so is suitable if you do not currently work within the electrical industry but who may wish to do so. The qualification will give you an opportunity to practice and be assessed in a secure environment on the installation of wiring systems together with the relevant theory of electrical installation. You will become familiar with the IET On-Site Guide and gain knowledge of electrical science and principles, to gain understanding of electrical circuits. This qualification does not make you an electrician but allows progression to further study.</p>",
